<h3 id="cc-rce">What the RCE paper states (OpenIE's own work)</h3>
<p>The following are from <a href="https://research.openie.dev/papers/rce/">the RCE paper</a> (version 1.24). They are listed here as the project's own work, not as a comparison with the projects above.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Canonical form.</strong> The canonical serialization is injective on Forms, so two Forms that differ have different shape hashes. Equivalence of behaviour is defined separately (fit equivalence), and in the engine's design equivalent variants are grouped by sound rewrites in an e-graph; the paper does not claim that equivalent behaviour always yields one canonical form.</li>
  <li><strong>Proofs.</strong> Determinism, totality, replay as a fold of the log, and atomicity of refused events are proved in Lean 4 on a core calculus. The Rust program emitter is proved on a core as a verified translation into MiniRust, a deep embedding of the emitted Rust subset; that the Rust compiler implements MiniRust is trusted and tested. This proof covers the program emitter, not the Form projection.</li>
  <li><strong>Gate.</strong> In the engine's design, a candidate passes replay of recorded inputs, a shadow run with a coverage bound, an output schema check and a Kani proof certificate, and a proposed rewrite also needs a Z3 proof. In the public record of one run, a local 1.5-billion-parameter model made 18 proposals, 13 of them distinct; the gate refused 15, and the 3 it admitted are one rewrite under three names that repeats a rule the engine already had.</li>
  <li><strong>Emit and lift.</strong> The reference checker emits Rust, Python and JavaScript, which each pass 1,459 conformance tests with 0 failures, and Scala, whose output does not yet agree with the reference evaluator; the emitters translate the checked program, not the Form. The only public lift from another language is a probe for one Go pattern. Lifting and emitting every language is the design goal of the proposal <code>spec/proposals/rce-form.md</code>, and nothing of that design is built.</li>
  <li><strong>Energy.</strong> In the engine's design every receipt carries <code>est_j</code>, a model; an unpriced model call is never read as zero. RCE has no measured energy figure: <code>measured_j</code> (wall meter) is empty in every result so far.</li>
</ul>

